--- !u!114 &1510873508
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1510873506}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: This scene provides a simplified setup for processing MIDI files. It
    uses the MidiFile behavior to import a binary MIDI file exported from a DAW.
    The data is then mapped to specific properties using MidiTween, which interpolates
    between an on and off value, similar to Tween.
  Warning: MIDI files must be renamed with the file extension ".bytes" for the asset
    to be imported correctly in Unity. Any other file extension will result in an
    unreadable file.
  URLTitle: MIDI Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/midi
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
